CON-08: keep a MASS-type load that reaches a node with no flow

addExternalInflows() books a MASS-type inflow (and a positive API mass
flux) as External Inflow and adds it to the node's mass accumulator, but
findStorageQual() (through getMixedQual) and findNodeQual() ignore the
accumulator when the node's inflow is at or below ZERO, so the load went
nowhere and the quality continuity error was 100 %. Mix such a load into
the stored water of a node that holds water; at a node that holds none,
book it as residue in Final Stored Mass, the way qualrout.c already books
the contents of a node or link that dries out. findNodeQual() takes the
time step for that.

Requires: NUM-45
Requires: NUM-46

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after NUM-45_swmm530.patch and NUM-46_swmm530.patch:
    git apply CON-08_swmm530.patch

